| `scripts/audit_dependencies_data.py` | Holds the closed vocabulary `scripts/audit_dependencies.py` keeps in the prose after a secret word in a diagnostic npm printed: `LINKING_WORDS`, `CAUSE_WORDS` (each mapped to the npm or Node.js message that holds it) and `CLAUSE_WORDS`, how many words of a clause are judged one at a time. A word not listed is hidden, so a value of a shape no one named is hidden rather than shown. It is data, not logic (CONVENTIONS §18). | imported by `scripts/audit_dependencies.py` | — | A word added here is shown wherever it follows a secret word, so a password that is one of these words is shown; add a word only from a message npm or Node.js prints. Not the accepted risks: those are `dependency_audit.accepted.<app>`. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md#16-dependency-audit-and-accepted-risks--scriptsaudit_dependenciespy) | always |
